{"\ufeffEmployee Leave Management (ELM)\nBusiness Rule Specifications \u2014 Final Synchronized v1.4\nFusion ERP \u2022 Employee Leave Management \u2022 Synchronized baseline v1.4\n\nRule discipline\nBusiness Rules externalize material policy, eligibility, authorization, calculation, routing, lifecycle, and threshold constraints. They constrain actor-triggered or event-triggered Use Cases and workflow transitions": null, " they are not workflow activities. BR-EL-021 and BR-EL-026 remain retired identifiers for traceability. BR-EL-030 uses current configured policy/hierarchy values": null, " holiday/RH calendar publication semantics remain under BR-EL-031.\n\n1. Business Rule Index\nBR ID\nRule Name\nType\nStatus\nRelated CFRs\nBR-EL-001\nSupported leave-category eligibility\nEligibility\nActive\nCFR-EL-002\u2013003\nBR-EL-002\nCasual Leave entitlement and lapse\nEntitlement\nActive\nCFR-EL-004, CFR-EL-028\nBR-EL-003\nRestricted Holiday entitlement and applicability\nEntitlement / Calendar\nActive\nCFR-EL-005, CFR-EL-025, CFR-EL-028\nBR-EL-004\nSpecial Casual Leave entitlement and admissibility\nEntitlement / Authority\nActive\nCFR-EL-006, CFR-EL-028\nBR-EL-005\nNon-faculty Earned Leave credit and carry-forward\nEntitlement\nActive\nCFR-EL-007, CFR-EL-028\nBR-EL-006\nFaculty Vacation Leave entitlement and vacation-period applicability\nEntitlement / Calendar\nActive\nCFR-EL-008\nBR-EL-007\nVL-to-EL year-end conversion\nCalculation / Year-end\nActive\nCFR-EL-008, CFR-EL-028\nBR-EL-008\nTreatment of EL created by VL conversion\nAccount\nActive\nCFR-EL-008, CFR-EL-028\nBR-EL-009\nCommuted Leave entitlement and treatment\nEntitlement / Evidence\nActive\nCFR-EL-009, CFR-EL-028\nBR-EL-010\nHalf-day CL treatment\nCalculation\nActive\nCFR-EL-004\nBR-EL-011\nContinuous-day counting\nCounting\nActive\nCFR-EL-003, CFR-EL-010\nBR-EL-012\nApplicant non-overlap with half-day CL exception\nValidation\nActive\nCFR-EL-003\nBR-EL-013\nStation Leave coupling\nScope / Information\nActive\nCFR-EL-002\nBR-EL-014\nSubstitute eligibility\nEligibility\nActive\nCFR-EL-011\u2013012\nBR-EL-015\nSubstitute consent gate and decline recovery\nRouting / Eligibility\nActive\nCFR-EL-012\nBR-EL-016\nUnit Head final scope for CL/RH\nAuthority\nActive\nCFR-EL-013, CFR-EL-019\nBR-EL-017\nUnit Head recommendation for higher-sanction leave\nAuthority / Routing\nActive\nCFR-EL-014, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nBR-EL-018\nHigher-sanction routing\nRouting\nActive\nCFR-EL-014, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nBR-EL-019\nAuthority resolution and optional Establishment step\nRouting / Authority\nActive\nCFR-EL-014, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nBR-EL-020\nDirector self-sanction\nAuthority / Exception\nActive\nCFR-EL-015\nBR-EL-021\nRETIRED \u2014 Modify Pending Request\nRetired\nRETIRED\n\u2014\nBR-EL-022\nImmediate withdrawal of pending request\nLifecycle\nActive\nCFR-EL-018\nBR-EL-023\nCancellation of approved leave before start\nLifecycle / Routing\nActive\nCFR-EL-019\nBR-EL-024\nFresh application after cancellation\nLifecycle\nActive\nCFR-EL-019\nBR-EL-025\nExtension of ongoing EL/COL/VL\nLifecycle / Calculation\nActive\nCFR-EL-020\nBR-EL-026\nRETIRED IDENTIFIER\nRetired\nRETIRED\n\u2014\nBR-EL-027\nResumption applicability and review authority\nLifecycle / Authority\nActive\nCFR-EL-021\nBR-EL-028\nNormal, early, and late resumption outcome\nLifecycle / Account\nActive\nCFR-EL-021\nBR-EL-029\nOffline-sanctioned leave synchronization\nRecord integrity\nActive\nCFR-EL-027\nBR-EL-030\nCurrent configured policy and hierarchy\nConfiguration\nActive\nCFR-EL-003, CFR-EL-014, CFR-EL-024\nBR-EL-031\nEffective published holiday/RH calendar\nCalendar\nActive\nCFR-EL-003, CFR-EL-005, CFR-EL-025\nBR-EL-032\nSLA reminder on still-pending task\nThreshold / Notification\nActive\nCFR-EL-031\nBR-EL-033\nSLA escalation on still-pending task\nThreshold / Escalation\nActive\nCFR-EL-032\nBR-EL-034\nNo post-submission modification\nLifecycle constraint\nActive\nCFR-EL-017\nBR-EL-035\nActionable task assignment notification\nNotification\nActive\nCFR-EL-030\nBR-EL-036\nRole-based authorization\nAuthorization\nActive\nCFR-EL-001\nBR-EL-037\nAdministrative maintenance is not sanctioning\nAuthorization / Record integrity\nActive\nCFR-EL-026\u2013027\nBR-EL-038\nConfigurable SLA thresholds\nConfiguration\nActive\nCFR-EL-029\n\n2. Rule Specifications\nBR-EL-001 \u2014 Supported leave-category eligibility\nRule Type\nEligibility\nRule Statement\nA new leave request shall use only CL, RH, SCL, EL, COL, or VL and shall satisfy the category-applicability conditions in the current configured ELM policy.\nApplies To\nNew leave validation\nCondition / Trigger\nRequested category/application context\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nReject/prevent progression when category applicability is not satisfied.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-002\u2013003\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-009\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\nStatus / Revision Note\nRevised to remove published-policy-version semantics.\n\nBR-EL-002 \u2014 Casual Leave entitlement and lapse\nRule Type\nEntitlement\nRule Statement\nEach employee has 8 CL days per year": null, " unused CL lapses at year end and does not carry forward.\nApplies To\nCL validation/year-end\nCondition / Trigger\nCL account/request\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nEnforce 8-day annual entitlement and no carry-forward.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-004, CFR-EL-028\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001": null, " EL-UC-020\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nActive.\n\nBR-EL-003 \u2014 Restricted Holiday entitlement and applicability\nRule Type\nEntitlement / Calendar\nRule Statement\nEach employee has 2 RH days per year": null, " an RH request must correspond to an applicable Restricted Holiday in the currently effective published holiday/RH calendar": null, " unused RH lapses at year end.\nApplies To\nRH validation/year-end\nCondition / Trigger\nRH request/account\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nEnforce entitlement, calendar applicability, and lapse.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-005, CFR-EL-025, CFR-EL-028\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-015": null, " EL-UC-020\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nExpanded/confirmed after adjudication.\n\nBR-EL-004 \u2014 Special Casual Leave entitlement and admissibility\nRule Type\nEntitlement / Authority\nRule Statement\nEach employee may use up to 15 SCL days per calendar year for a special purpose considered admissible by the applicable Sanctioning Authority": null, " no separate encoded admissibility criterion is required": null, " unused SCL lapses at year end.\nApplies To\nSCL validation/decision/year-end\nCondition / Trigger\nSCL request/account\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nEnforce annual limit": null, " leave purpose is judged by authority": null, " lapse unused SCL.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-006, CFR-EL-028\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-005": null, " EL-UC-020\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nClarified: admissibility is authority judgment, not separate encoded rule.\n\nBR-EL-005 \u2014 Non-faculty Earned Leave credit and carry-forward\nRule Type\nEntitlement\nRule Statement\nEach non-faculty employee shall receive 30 EL days per year and unused EL shall carry forward according to policy.\nApplies To\nEL account/year-end\nCondition / Trigger\nNon-faculty EL\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nCredit 30/year and preserve unused EL across year boundary.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-007, CFR-EL-028\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001": null, " EL-UC-020\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nActive.\n\nBR-EL-006 \u2014 Faculty Vacation Leave entitlement and vacation-period applicability\nRule Type\nEntitlement / Calendar\nRule Statement\nEach faculty member shall have 60 VL associated with vacation periods supplied by the institute Academic Calendar, and VL may be availed only during an applicable vacation period.\nApplies To\nVL validation\nCondition / Trigger\nFaculty VL request\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nEnforce 60 VL and external Academic Calendar vacation-period applicability.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-008\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nClarified external vacation-period source.\n\nBR-EL-007 \u2014 VL-to-EL year-end conversion\nRule Type\nCalculation / Year-end\nRule Statement\nAt year end, all unused faculty VL shall convert to EL at 2 VL : 1 EL including fractional conversion, and VL itself shall not carry forward.\nApplies To\nYear-end processing\nCondition / Trigger\nUnused faculty VL\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nConvert at 2:1 including fractions": null, " leave no unused VL balance as VL.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-008, CFR-EL-028\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-020\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\nStatus / Revision Note\nActive, consolidated statement.\n\nBR-EL-008 \u2014 Treatment of EL created by VL conversion\nRule Type\nAccount\nRule Statement\nEL created by VL conversion shall be credited to the faculty member's EL balance, may carry forward, and may subsequently be availed.\nApplies To\nYear-end/account use\nCondition / Trigger\nConverted EL\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nCredit and retain converted EL as usable EL.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-008, CFR-EL-028\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-020": null, " EL-UC-001\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\nStatus / Revision Note\nActive.\n\nBR-EL-009 \u2014 Commuted Leave entitlement and treatment\nRule Type\nEntitlement / Evidence\nRule Statement\nEligible employees have 20 COL days/year in this baseline": null, " COL is medical/balance-controlled, supporting medical evidence may be required where applicable, and unused COL carries forward.\nApplies To\nCOL validation/year-end\nCondition / Trigger\nCOL request/account\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nEnforce annual entitlement, balance/evidence conditions, and carry-forward.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-009, CFR-EL-028\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001": null, " EL-UC-020\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nConsolidated.\n\nBR-EL-010 \u2014 Half-day CL treatment\nRule Type\nCalculation\nRule Statement\nCL shall support first-half and second-half requests": null, " an approved half day consumes 0.5 CL day.\nApplies To\nCL validation/accounting\nCondition / Trigger\nHalf-day CL\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nRecognize halves and deduct 0.5 day when approved.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-004\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nActive.\n\nBR-EL-011 \u2014 Continuous-day counting\nRule Type\nCounting\nRule Statement\nFor EL, COL, and VL, intervening weekends and closed holidays inside the continuous approved interval count as leave days": null, " this rule does not apply to CL, SCL, or RH.\nApplies To\nLeave-day calculation\nCondition / Trigger\nEL/COL/VL and excluded categories\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nApply category-specific counting boundary exactly.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-003, CFR-EL-010\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-009\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\nStatus / Revision Note\nActive.\n\nBR-EL-012 \u2014 Applicant non-overlap with half-day CL exception\nRule Type\nValidation\nRule Statement\nA new request shall not impermissibly overlap the employee's active pending or approved leave": null, " first-half and second-half CL on the same date are non-overlapping when they occupy different halves.\nApplies To\nNew-request validation\nCondition / Trigger\nEmployee leave intervals\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nBlock impermissible overlap": null, " permit different CL halves on same date.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-003\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nConfirmed PS gap.\n\nBR-EL-013 \u2014 Station Leave coupling\nRule Type\nScope / Information\nRule Statement\nStation Leave permission/details, when applicable, shall be captured within the same leave application and shall not create a separate leave-request process.\nApplies To\nLeave application\nCondition / Trigger\nOutside-Jabalpur context\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nKeep Station Leave inside associated leave application.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-002\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nActive.\n\nBR-EL-014 \u2014 Substitute eligibility\nRule Type\nEligibility\nRule Statement\nWhen responsibility coverage is required, exactly one substitute is nominated": null, " the substitute must be another employee, must not be the applicant, and must have no overlapping pending or approved leave during the responsibility period.\nApplies To\nSubstitute nomination\nCondition / Trigger\nNominated employee and responsibility period\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nReject an ineligible nominee.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-011\u2013012\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-002, EL-UC-009, EL-UC-019\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\nStatus / Revision Note\nExpanded to include not-the-applicant condition.\n\nBR-EL-015 \u2014 Substitute consent gate and decline recovery\nRule Type\nRouting / Eligibility\nRule Statement\nRequired approval routing shall not proceed until the nominated substitute accepts. A decline leaves the consent gate closed": null, " the applicant may nominate another eligible substitute or withdraw the pending request where applicable.\nApplies To\nSubstitute response\nCondition / Trigger\nPending request requiring responsibility coverage\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nAccept releases routing gate": null, " decline does not.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-012\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-002, EL-UC-019\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\nStatus / Revision Note\nExpanded with adjudicated recovery path.\n\nBR-EL-016 \u2014 Unit Head final scope for CL/RH\nRule Type\nAuthority\nRule Statement\nFor CL and RH, including associated Station Leave, the applicant's Unit Head is the final approve/reject authority except for the Director-specific self-sanction case.\nApplies To\nNew leave / same-hierarchy cancellation\nCondition / Trigger\nCL/RH request\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nFinal decision is made at Unit Head unless Director exception applies.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-013, CFR-EL-019\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-003, EL-UC-008\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-02\nStatus / Revision Note\nActive.\n\nBR-EL-017 \u2014 Unit Head recommendation for higher-sanction leave\nRule Type\nAuthority / Routing\nRule Statement\nFor SCL, EL, COL, and VL, the Unit Head records Recommended or Not Recommended": null, " Not Recommended is not a final rejection and both outcomes continue through the applicable higher-sanction path.\nApplies To\nHigher-sanction new leave/extension/cancellation\nCondition / Trigger\nHigher-sanction request\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nRecord recommendation and continue routing.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-014, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-003\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-02": null, " CW-EL-03\nStatus / Revision Note\nClarified after adjudication.\n\nBR-EL-018 \u2014 Higher-sanction routing\nRule Type\nRouting\nRule Statement\nSCL, EL, COL, and VL requests requiring higher sanction shall proceed through the current configured hierarchy to the resolved final Sanctioning Authority.\nApplies To\nHigher-sanction contexts\nCondition / Trigger\nRouted request\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nRoute to competent final authority using current configuration.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-014, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-003\u2013005\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\nStatus / Revision Note\nRevised to current configuration terminology.\n\nBR-EL-019 \u2014 Authority resolution and optional Establishment step\nRule Type\nRouting / Authority\nRule Statement\nThe processing/sanctioning path shall be resolved from applicant, organizational unit, designation/role, leave category, and current hierarchy configuration": null, " an Establishment step and the roles Deputy Registrar (Estt.), Dean, Registrar, and Director occur only where configured.\nApplies To\nRouting resolution\nCondition / Trigger\nHigher-sanction request\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nResolve and use only configured processing/authority steps.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-014, CFR-EL-019\u2013020\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-003\u2013005\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\nStatus / Revision Note\nRevised to remove effective-published-policy wording.\n\nBR-EL-020 \u2014 Director self-sanction\nRule Type\nAuthority / Exception\nRule Statement\nWhen the Director is the applicant, the Director-specific self-sanction path replaces the normal Unit Head/higher-authority route.\nApplies To\nDirector-applicant leave\nCondition / Trigger\nApplicant role ": "Director\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nUse Director self-sanction path.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-015\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-005\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nActive.\n\nBR-EL-021 \u2014 RETIRED \u2014 Modify Pending Request\nRule Type\nRetired\nRule Statement\nThe former rule permitting pending-request modification is retired. Post-submission modification is not part of the synchronized baseline.\nApplies To\nN/A\nCondition / Trigger\nN/A\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nN/A\nRelated CFRs\n\u2014\nRelated Use Cases\n\u2014\nRelated Workflow(s)\n\u2014\nStatus / Revision Note\nRetired because G-09 reversed the former semantics", " replacement is BR-EL-034.\n\nBR-EL-022 \u2014 Immediate withdrawal of pending request\nRule Type\nLifecycle\nRule Statement\nA pending request may be withdrawn at any time before final approval": null, " withdrawal is immediate, terminates remaining approval processing, blocks later approve/reject actions, and informs concerned roles. After final approval, withdrawal is unavailable.\nApplies To\nPending request lifecycle\nCondition / Trigger\nPending before final approval\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nApply immediate terminal withdrawal effects.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-018\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-007\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nConsolidated and strengthened.\n\nBR-EL-023 \u2014 Cancellation of approved leave before start\nRule Type\nLifecycle / Routing\nRule Statement\nAn approved leave may be cancelled only before its start date": null, " cancellation uses the same applicable hierarchy, does not edit the approved leave in place, approval marks the leave Cancelled and restores/adjusts already deducted balance, while rejection leaves the original approval unchanged.\nApplies To\nApproved-leave cancellation\nCondition / Trigger\nApproved and not started\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nEnforce pre-start boundary and context-specific final effects.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-019\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-008, EL-UC-003\u2013005\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-02\nStatus / Revision Note\nExpanded with adjudicated outcome effects.\n\nBR-EL-024 \u2014 Fresh application after cancellation\nRule Type\nLifecycle\nRule Statement\nIf revised leave is still required after cancellation, a fresh leave application shall be submitted rather than editing the approved leave in place.\nApplies To\nApproved-leave change\nCondition / Trigger\nSuccessful cancellation followed by revised need\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nRequire fresh application.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-019\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-008, EL-UC-001\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-02\nStatus / Revision Note\nActive.\n\nBR-EL-025 \u2014 Extension of ongoing EL/COL/VL\nRule Type\nLifecycle / Calculation\nRule Statement\nExtension is available only for ongoing EL/COL/VL": null, " it uses applicable eligibility, balance, substitute, calendar and sanction rules": null, " approval posts only the incremental additional period while rejection preserves the original approved leave.\nApplies To\nOngoing leave extension\nCondition / Trigger\nOngoing EL/COL/VL\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nValidate/rout appropriately and apply incremental-only approval effect.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-020\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-009, EL-UC-002\u2013005, EL-UC-019\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-03\nStatus / Revision Note\nExpanded with adjudicated incremental-posting rule.\n\nBR-EL-026 \u2014 RETIRED IDENTIFIER\nRule Type\nRetired\nRule Statement\nNo active rule is assigned to this identifier.\nApplies To\nN/A\nCondition / Trigger\nN/A\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nN/A\nRelated CFRs\n\u2014\nRelated Use Cases\n\u2014\nRelated Workflow(s)\n\u2014\nStatus / Revision Note\nRemains retired.\n\nBR-EL-027 \u2014 Resumption applicability and review authority\nRule Type\nLifecycle / Authority\nRule Statement\nFormal resumption review applies to EL, COL, and VL": null, " the employee submits actual resumption information and the applicable Sanctioning Authority reviews it.\nApplies To\nResumption\nCondition / Trigger\nReturn from EL/COL/VL\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nRoute submitted resumption to applicable Sanctioning Authority.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-021\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-010\u2013011\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-04\nStatus / Revision Note\nRevised verifier identity.\n\nBR-EL-028 \u2014 Normal, early, and late resumption outcome\nRule Type\nLifecycle / Account\nRule Statement\nIf actual resumption equals the approved end date, review causes no adjustment to approved leave period or balance. If actual resumption is earlier or later, after review ELM records the actual leave period, adjusts leave balance accordingly, and synchronizes relevant leave/attendance records.\nApplies To\nResumption review\nCondition / Trigger\nCompare actual vs approved end date\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nApply no-adjustment or adjusted synchronization branch.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-021\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-011\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-04\nStatus / Revision Note\nMajor revision: no generic closure state": null, " late resumption explicitly supported.\n\nBR-EL-029 \u2014 Offline-sanctioned leave synchronization\nRule Type\nRecord integrity\nRule Statement\nOnly leave already sanctioned through an authorized offline/paper process may be retrospectively recorded": null, " sanction/reference evidence shall be captured, record consistency validated, relevant balance/history synchronized, and no second approval workflow initiated.\nApplies To\nOffline leave entry\nCondition / Trigger\nAlready-sanctioned leave + acceptable ELM-unavailable context\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nSynchronize records without new sanction.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-027\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-016\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\nStatus / Revision Note\nExpanded with evidence and consistency requirements.\n\nBR-EL-030 \u2014 Current configured policy and hierarchy\nRule Type\nConfiguration\nRule Statement\nELM validation and routing shall use the current configured leave-policy parameters and hierarchy configuration. No draft/publish/effective-version lifecycle applies to leave-policy parameters in this baseline.\nApplies To\nValidation/routing/admin config\nCondition / Trigger\nCurrent configured values\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nUse current configuration directly": null, " do not depend on policy publication state.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-003, CFR-EL-014, CFR-EL-024\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-003\u2013005, EL-UC-014\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03\nStatus / Revision Note\nMaterially revised from former 'Effective Policy Version' rule.\n\nBR-EL-031 \u2014 Effective published holiday/RH calendar\nRule Type\nCalendar\nRule Statement\nDate and RH validation shall use the currently effective published holiday/RH calendar until a replacement calendar is published.\nApplies To\nDate/RH validation\nCondition / Trigger\nPublished calendar state\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nUse current published calendar": null, " activate replacement only when published.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-003, CFR-EL-005, CFR-EL-025\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-015\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nConfirmed after adjudication.\n\nBR-EL-032 \u2014 SLA reminder on still-pending task\nRule Type\nThreshold / Notification\nRule Statement\nWhen an SLA-controlled actionable task reaches its configured reminder threshold, issue a reminder to the responsible user and log it only if the task is still pending": null, " otherwise issue no reminder.\nApplies To\nEL-UC-021 / SLA reminder-threshold processing\nCondition / Trigger\nTask at reminder threshold\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nPending -> remind+log": null, " non-pending -> no reminder.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-031\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-021\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A \u2014 reminder alone does not create a workflow transition.\nStatus / Revision Note\nStrengthened with pending-only guard.\n\nBR-EL-033 \u2014 SLA escalation on still-pending task\nRule Type\nThreshold / Escalation\nRule Statement\nWhen an SLA-controlled actionable task remains pending past its configured escalation threshold, the system shall perform the configured escalation action: notify the configured higher/responsible authority and, where the escalation configuration changes routing/responsibility, apply that routing/responsibility change": null, " the escalation action shall be logged. If the task is no longer pending, no escalation shall be issued.\nApplies To\nEL-UC-021 / SLA escalation-threshold processing\nCondition / Trigger\nTask past escalation threshold\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nPending -> configured notify/escalate action + log": null, " non-pending -> no escalation.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-032\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-021\nRelated Workflow(s)\nConditional cross-cutting trace to the applicable CW-EL-01\u201304 only when escalation changes routing/responsibility": null, " notification-only escalation ": "N/A.\nStatus / Revision Note\nPending-only guard retained", " notification-only and routing/responsibility-changing escalation are distinguished formally.\n\nBR-EL-034 \u2014 No post-submission modification\nRule Type\nLifecycle constraint\nRule Statement\nA submitted pending leave request shall not be modified in place. If change is needed before final approval, the employee may withdraw and submit a new application if needed.\nApplies To\nPending request\nCondition / Trigger\nSubmitted and pending\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nBlock in-place modification": null, " preserve withdrawal/new-application route.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-017\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-007, EL-UC-001\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01\nStatus / Revision Note\nNew replacement rule for retired BR-EL-021.\n\nBR-EL-035 \u2014 Actionable task assignment notification\nRule Type\nNotification\nRule Statement\nWhen an actionable workflow task is assigned to a user, ELM shall notify the assigned user.\nApplies To\nTask assignment\nCondition / Trigger\nNew actionable assignment\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nGenerate assignment notification.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-030\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-002\u2013005, EL-UC-011": null, " EL-UC-021\nRelated Workflow(s)\nCW-EL-01": null, " CW-EL-03": null, " CW-EL-04\nStatus / Revision Note\nNew explicit rule from adjudicated PS.\n\nBR-EL-036 \u2014 Role-based authorization\nRule Type\nAuthorization\nRule Statement\nELM capabilities shall be available only to users authorized for the corresponding employee, processing, sanctioning, or administrative role.\nApplies To\nAll protected ELM actions\nCondition / Trigger\nAttempted protected action\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nPermit only role-authorized action.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-001\nRelated Use Cases\nAll actor UCs\nRelated Workflow(s)\nAll composite workflows\nStatus / Revision Note\nNew explicit cross-cutting rule from PS.\n\nBR-EL-037 \u2014 Administrative maintenance is not sanctioning\nRule Type\nAuthorization / Record integrity\nRule Statement\nAuthorized leave-record maintenance/correction shall not itself create a new sanctioning decision": null, " retrospective offline entry is also synchronization rather than a second approval.\nApplies To\nAdministrative record maintenance\nCondition / Trigger\nAdmin maintenance action\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nPreserve separation between record maintenance and sanctioning.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-026\u2013027\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-016\u2013017\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\nStatus / Revision Note\nNew explicit cross-cutting distinction.\n\nBR-EL-038 \u2014 Configurable SLA thresholds\nRule Type\nConfiguration\nRule Statement\nReminder and escalation thresholds for SLA-controlled actionable workflow tasks shall be configurable by an authorized administrative role and shall govern EL-UC-021 event-triggered SLA processing.\nApplies To\nSLA configuration\nCondition / Trigger\nAuthorized threshold change\nRequired Outcome / Constraint\nStore valid thresholds and use them in EL-UC-021.\nRelated CFRs\nCFR-EL-029\nRelated Use Cases\nEL-UC-018": null, " EL-UC-021\nRelated Workflow(s)\nN/A\nStatus / Revision Note\nNew explicit configuration rule.": null}